 \subsection{Safety Across Reordering and Model Changes}
 \label{sec:eval-safety}
 
 We first reorder reads on purpose. In six controlled tests, engine~A's input-consumed event completes before graph~B submits its reads. Under stream-only release, the graph's outputs matched the replacement frame in every test, because recording stream use cannot cover reads that have not been submitted~\cite{recordstream}; under BIM and Manual, they matched the admitted frame. Under load, each of the 109,592 results delivered by BIM, Manual, and Full in the 144 rate and late-read runs carried its admitted identity and matched the reference outputs.
 
-We then change the models. Across eight graph snapshots per model, three inputs, and two methods, regenerated boundaries kept all 96 ordered-overwrite cases exact against unsplit references, and binding validation rejected each of 22 attempted substitutions of plan, code, globals, model state, or input before the affected stage ran.
+We then change the models. In 96 ordered-overwrite cases (eight graph snapshots per model, three inputs, and two methods), the source was overwritten once the regenerated boundary had completed, and every output still matched the unsplit model's exactly. Binding validation rejected each of 22 attempted substitutions of plan, code, globals, model state, or input before the affected stage ran.
 
-Finally, we replay 16 controlled transitions: 14 graph edits, one batch-normalization folding, and a public ResNet-18 to ResNet-50 substitution, whose binding check runs on the CPU. The runtime release point moves in 13 of them; folding keeps the head's first source read, and the two alias-chain edits only renumber operations (Fig.~\ref{fig:boundaries}). Binding checks reject every outdated hand-placed plan, so a manual deployment stops until someone refreshes its plan. ReadSeal rebuilds the updated plans in 0.08--0.21\,s on the CPU, with no source-reader or boundary annotations. In the mixed-recipient campaign, adding a late read likewise made Manual-checked's old boundary fail its check until the boundary was moved, after which all 24 update cases gave exact outputs.
